@startuml outbox
title The transactional outbox — one transaction, two facts

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"

participant "Command handler" as H
participant "AppDbContext" as Ctx
participant "DomainEventsToOutboxInterceptor" as Int
database "postgres" as Pg
participant "OutboxProcessor\n(worker)" as Out
queue "kafka" as K

H -> Ctx : users.Add(user)\ninvitations.Add(invitation)
note right of H
  The aggregate raised
  UserInvitedDomainEvent.
  Nothing is published here.
end note

H -> Ctx : SaveChangesAsync()
activate Ctx
Ctx -> Int : SavingChanges
activate Int
Int -> Int : drain domain events\ntranslate to integration events
Int -> Ctx : add OutboxMessage rows
deactivate Int
Ctx -> Pg : BEGIN\n  INSERT users\n  INSERT invitations\n  INSERT outbox_messages\nCOMMIT
deactivate Ctx

note over Pg
  The state change and the intent to
  publish commit together, or neither
  does. No dual write.
end note

Out -> Pg : SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
activate Out
Out -> K : publish
Out -> Pg : set processed_at
deactivate Out

note right of Out
  At-least-once: the broker may ack
  immediately before the row is marked.
  Every event carries a stable EventId
  so consumers can deduplicate.
end note

@enduml
